{"text": "RSLC REDMAP 2.0\n2012 Cycle Timeline\n\nPost Op:\n~--2010 Budget - $20m vs. $10m, vs. $30 m total budget Ed has been quoted on...\n~-Timetable \u2014 last 6 months of the cycle is not optimum, but we capitalized on the unique environment.\n--Limited historical corporate and individual support at upper brackets.\n--AXR \u2014 the money we earlier anticipated was not there.\n--Individual Support - former RNC donors could not be cultivated within the short time-frame, to a lesser\nknown entity and so late in cycle. [Many were solidly with the RGA, etc.]\n--Activity level \u2014 In general, activity level was sufficient \u2014 we did compete with other EG clients for time and\ntravel activity.\n--List out accomplishments for REDMAP and RSLC as a whole\n--Tough to build awareness at the same time you are developing infrastructure to support the future and\nraise money for current program. Even Ed was surprised at level of awareness of RSLC.\n--We talked briefly about the disclosure issue in raising money for REDMAP. The extent at which\ncompanies and individuals were concerned over disclosure and wanting c4 cover was far greater than\nexpected,\n--A good amount of $ went elsewhere to help us, but also to help others. Some elected to give no support.\n--Other avenues for support \u2014 membership money and RLCC political money, Special vs. Gold money, AJP,\nspecial money for LE\u2019s, etc.\n\nDiscussion Points:\n--Chairman\u2019s program vision post redistricting, women and Hispanic initiative/next steps...\n--Meeting with Ed before December group meeting to gain his post election, pos-REDMAP vision on\nChairman\u2019s Program 2.0 REDMAP. This could get us more focused for the December meeting, maybe to\ninclude preliminary materials.\n--Do we create ac4?\n--Do we formalize any informal relationships from 2010?\n--What are ways we should structurally change to make 2012 more effective/efficient than 2010?\n\n2011 Work:\n--Comprehensive Game Plan ~ Nationally by state -- not by program or money type.\n--REDMAP Support as Renewals \u2014 Allow REDMAP supporters to weigh in on 2.0 projects by stressing the\nneed for $$ in Year I to support candidate recruitment-- especially of women and minorities. Within\nmaterials, we need to answer the question \u2014 \u2018with early $, the Chairman could do X, Y, Z... which was not\npossible for REDMAP kicking off last year?\n--Write up state-wide success stories to carry forth the other states, i.e. PA, OH, NC, N\u00a5(?), CO, TX, CA (AG\nrace?)\n--National Fundraising Committee \u2014i.e. regional fundraisers early, steering committee of women and\nminorities, regional fundraising committee (the individual money people).",
